{"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/coloringstrategy"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ColoringStrategy"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyColoring(strategy:)"},{"text":" orders the vertices. Each vertex in turn takes the least colour","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"none of its already coloured neighbours has (first fit). Degrees are simple degrees (distinct","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other neighbours, self-loops left out); ties go to the lesser vertex index, except for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".coloredNeighbors"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/coloredNeighbors","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialBreadthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/connectedSequentialDepthFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/independentSet","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/largestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/saturationLargestFirst","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/ColoringStrategy\/smallestLast"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","gen